<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10510" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consĭlĭārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		consilium, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>suitable for counsel, counselling</i> (class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ep. 1, 2, 56</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magis consiliarius amicus quam auxiliarius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Truc. 2, 1, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">particeps,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Mil. 4, 2, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					18, 3, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fulgur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 2, 39, 1</span></i>
			; cf. Müll. Etrusk. 2, p. 168.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consĭlĭārĭus</span></b> ,
				ĭi, m., <i>a
				counsellor, adviser</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consiliario et auctore Vestorio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 14, 9, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 19, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(Verris) amici et consiliarii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Verr. 2, 2, 17, § 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 1, 2, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">AVGVSTI,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 2648</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caedis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vell.
					2, 56</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Esp. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> T. t.,
				<i>an assessor, aid in a court of justice</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 55</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Claud. 12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Of the augur as the <i>interpreter</i> of
			the divine will: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consiliarius atque administer Jovis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Leg. 3, 19, 43</span></i>
			.</div>
